From 3e8a97d0ebd161eceb934175a5fba5fd23f71ad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shreenidhi Shedi <shreenidhi.shedi@broadcom.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:33:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix: use Meson's libexecdir for ds-identify and SSH key
 fingerprints

Use the Meson-configured helper directory (recorded in
cloudinit/meson_paths.py) for ds-identify, write-ssh-key-fingerprints,
and the executable temporary-directory fallback, so cloud-init finds
its installed tools when libexecdir differs from /usr/lib.

Set usr_lib_exec = "/usr/libexec" in the Photon distro class; Photon
installs helpers under /usr/libexec, not the default /usr/lib.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Shreenidhi Shedi <shreenidhi.shedi@broadcom.com>
